  "ingredients": [
    "128 ounce pork loin back ribs",
    "3 tablespoon salt",
    "3 tablespoon black pepper",
    "1 tablespoon garlic powder",
    "1 tablespoon chipotle seasoning (such as Tone's)",
    "3 tablespoon liquid smoke",
    "1 1/2 cup smoker chips (such as Char-Broil)",
    "1/2 cup low-carb ketchup",
    "1 tablespoon hot sauce",
    "2 teaspoon yellow mustard",
    "1 teaspoon liquid smoke",
    "1 teaspoon worcestershire sauce",
    "1/2 teaspoon all-purpose seasoning (such as Mrs. Dash)",
    "1/2 teaspoon chili powder",
    "1/2 teaspoon cumin",
    "1/4 teaspoon cayenne pepper"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat oven to 225F. Remove the silverskin from the ribs (which is easiest done by hand).",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pork-loin-ribs-keto-bbq-sauce/#wprm-recipe-50785-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/pork-ribs-keto-bbq-sauce-01.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Season well on both sides with the salt, pepper, garlic powder, Southwest seasoning, and liquid smoke.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pork-loin-ribs-keto-bbq-sauce/#wprm-recipe-50785-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/pork-ribs-keto-bbq-sauce-03.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place the ribs on a large baking pan and cover with foil. Bake for 2 hours in the oven. Turn the oven up to 250F and bake for a further 2 hours. Once done, remove from the oven. The ribs will look cooked but plain.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pork-loin-ribs-keto-bbq-sauce/#wprm-recipe-50785-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Mix together the ketchup, hot sauce, mustard, liquid smoke, Worcestershire sauce, seasoning blend, chili powder, cumin, and cayenne pepper.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pork-loin-ribs-keto-bbq-sauce/#wprm-recipe-50785-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/pork-ribs-keto-bbq-sauce-04.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Soak the wood chips.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pork-loin-ribs-keto-bbq-sauce/#wprm-recipe-50785-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/pork-ribs-keto-bbq-sauce-06.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lay the meat on a new sheet of foil.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pork-loin-ribs-keto-bbq-sauce/#wprm-recipe-50785-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/pork-ribs-keto-bbq-sauce-10.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Brush the ribs liberally on both sides with about half of the BBQ sauce. A silicone basting brush works well here.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pork-loin-ribs-keto-bbq-sauce/#wprm-recipe-50785-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/pork-ribs-keto-bbq-sauce-11.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the smoker chips to a smoker. Place the smoker on a grill over medium-high heat (the heat should be over the smokebox only, not the meat). Smoke for at least 60 minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pork-loin-ribs-keto-bbq-sauce/#wprm-recipe-50785-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/pork-ribs-keto-bbq-sauce-12.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Once the ribs are done smoking, turn up the heat underneath the ribs. Cook on each side for about 10 minutes, basting some BBQ sauce over them, if desired. I save my sauce for the end. Let rest for about 5–10 minutes. Slice and serve with the remaining BBQ sauce. Enjoy!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pork-loin-ribs-keto-bbq-sauce/#wprm-recipe-50785-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/pork-ribs-keto-bbq-sauce-13.jpg"
    }
  ],
